  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "For each a in {1,3}, there exists an integer N_a such that c_{6,(0,a)}(n)>0 for every integer n>=N_a, with c_{6,(0,a)} normalized and interpreted as in problem.md. Equivalently, each of the two Gerber--Norton e=6 charged-core coefficient sequences has only finitely many zero coefficients. This does not assert an effective value of N_a and does not settle positivity in every degree.",
